n. If the secret is 17, Daniel (17) is 0, Leonora (15) is off by 2, Me (12) is off by 5. Daniel wins. The midpoint of the *overlap* is usually the best Bayesian estimate if ranges are independent and uniform. Overlap is 1-24. Midpoint 12.5. I will guess 13 (rounding up) or 12. Let's go with 13. It's close to the center of the overlap and distinct from Daniel and Leonora's likely guesses.",
